   "evidence": "They extend `Sobolev/Local/Reflection.lean:559 HasWeakLineDerivOn.setIntegral_fderiv_smul_eq_neg` and `Sobolev/Local/Reflection/Odd.lean:160 ..._of_continuousOn`. Their only other dependencies are `Sobolev/Leibniz.lean:425 HasWeakLineDerivOn.contDiffOn_clm_apply_of_ne_zero`, `Calculus/BumpFunction/Cutoff.lean:163` and `Distribution/TestFunction/LineDeriv.lean:169`. They use no `crFormalAdjoint`, `IsSobolevCRCoefficients` or `IsWeakCRSolutionHalf`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Complex/CauchyRiemann/RoughCoefficients/HalfPlane/Green.lean",
   "fix": "Move them into the Sobolev layer next to `HasWeakLineDerivOn.setIntegral_fderiv_smul_eq_neg_of_continuousOn` (`Sobolev/Local/Reflection/Odd.lean`, or a new `Sobolev/Local/Reflection/` file importing `Sobolev.Leibniz`, `BumpFunction.Cutoff` and `TestFunction.LineDeriv`), with the helpers made public. Green.lean keeps only the `crFormalAdjoint` results and imports the new location.",
   "issue": "`HasWeakLineDerivOn.setIntegral_im_pos_eq_zero` (l.111) and `setIntegral_im_pos_inner_fderiv_eq_neg` (l.148), plus the private helpers `memLpLoc_one_inner`, `integrableOn_im_pos_inner` and `integrableOn_im_pos_inner_fderiv` (l.72-104), are general half-plane integration by parts for weakly differentiable functions with no CR content. They sit in a CR-specific file, so other half-plane boundary problems would have to import CR theory to use them; `private` hides the helpers instead of placing them correctly.",
   "line": 111
  }
